# Git Commit Rules

## Don't run git commit
Don't run `git commit` (including `--amend`) unless the repo's own rules say the agent may commit there. In that case, show the message and wait for approval before each commit.

## Workflow
1. Stage files when the user says to stage
2. After staging, give the commit message as one paste-ready `git -C <abs repo path> commit -F - <<'EOF'` command
3. Stop. The user runs the commit themselves.
4. After the user says "pushed", read and follow the `update-pr` skill to offer creating or updating the PR.

## Commit message style
- Commitizen (git-cz) style: `<type>: <emoji> <subject>`, for example `feat: 🎸 add jira-cli to Brewfile`
- Types and emojis: `feat` 🎸, `fix` 🐛, `refactor` 💡, `docs` ✏️, `style` 💄, `test` 💍, `perf` ⚡️, `chore` 🤖, `ci` 🎡
- Subject in lowercase imperative mood, no filler, no trailing period

## Never suggest or add
- `Co-authored-by` trailers of any kind
- `--author` flags referencing AI tools
